Declare the Scala target's host vocabulary as a definition and list Local among Draco's members

Dev accepted, on 2026-10-21, "the bootstrap host vocabulary as a definition-backed member of
draco.scalatarget carrying [(Text, TypeName)] binding pairs, supplied explicitly to load and
Generate, with Local listed as a Draco member." The two-stage loader had measured the need: the
canonical corpus resolves only with 41 host names no draco domain defines, and that list lived in
a test.

draco.scalatarget.HostBindings is the new trio beside CirceCodecs: four global lists in the form
TransformBinding.nameBindings already carries — primitives, collections, seams (circe, java, scala.io,
scala.util, evrete, pekko) and the hand-written engine (DracoGenerator, draco.Drake, NameResolution)
— concatenated as `bindings`, with `vocabulary` their map. Each pair is the name as the corpus
authors it and the identity the Scala target realizes it as; a name a draco type shadows
(Encoder, Decoder, Knowledge, Source, Drake) is keyed qualified, since the ontology would win the
bare form, and a qualified reference resolves by identity whatever the key. The vocabulary is
supplied explicitly: DomainBuilder.load takes it as its bindings, Generate through
TransformBinding.nameBindings; nothing defaults to it and nothing discovers it, so another target
supplies its own table for the same authored names and no definition file carries a target spelling.

Local, the one TypeElement kind absent from Draco's `types` list, is listed, so `draco.Local`
resolves through the ontology; the loading test pins that and that neither Unit nor Local is a
binding. Draco.scala and ScalaTarget.scala regenerate on their member lists; HostBindings.scala is
generated. DomainLoadingTest reads the vocabulary from the definition. One new corpus type: parse
scope 110 draco + 10 mods, one loss across 120 types, 110 aspect sections, GenDrake 108 of 108;
every other headline unchanged (table updated in this commit). Shortening the bootstrap files
remains a later step.

Probe on the compiled engine over a resource overlay, nineteen suites including the three trio
gates, the example map, SourceContract, GenDrake, both aspect suites, the scenario, loading,
resolution, builder, ontology, the four dreams suites and both assembly suites: 689 passed, zero
failed or aborted, pending mods actors 0.

